Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 23:21:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 09/29] perf(chunk/compact): bounded concurrency in compaction
 cycles

Closes #8 (gqf2008/brewfs)

run_compaction_cycle processed up to max_chunks_per_run chunks fully
serially (should_compact -> lock -> compact), even though CompactConfig
already declared max_concurrent_tasks.

- CompactionWorkerConfig gains max_concurrent_tasks (default 4) and
  VfsBackgroundConfig::from_compact_config propagates CompactConfig's
  value.
- run_compaction_cycle now runs up to max_concurrent_tasks independent
  chunks concurrently (semaphore acquired before spawn). Chunks in one
  cycle are distinct and the per-chunk global lock is unchanged, so the
  same chunk can never be compacted twice.
- Tests: default concurrency >= 1; propagation from CompactConfig.
